cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "NURG_Fault_Analysis: Python scripts, interpreted faults and horizons for the 3D seismic analysis of the central northern Upper Rhine Graben"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MairJ/NURG_Fault_Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Python scripts for Expansion Index, fault throw and thickness analysis, together with the
  interpreted fault surfaces and stratigraphic horizons (depth domain) used in the manuscript
  "Movement history of faults under variable stress fields - insights derived from 3D seismics
  in the central northern Upper Rhine Graben, Germany". The 3D seismic reflection data are not
  included; they are available from the Hessian Agency for Nature Conservation, Environment
  and Geology (HLNUG) under the Geologiedatengesetz.
keywords:
  - Upper Rhine Graben
  - 3D seismic
  - fault growth
  - expansion index
  - throw analysis
  - structural geology
